+// The lobby's first screen and the Quests page on a phone (sections 32a to 32h).
+//   32a  a game tile is on the first screen of the lobby at 7 window sizes (and as much as fits on a small phone and on phones held sideways)
+//   32b  the Live tables strip is still there, one row lower: four cards that are links to real tables, and "All tables"
+//   32c  the welcome banners and the house-edge strip keep every sentence and every link (shown in full, not clipped), wherever they are drawn
+//   32d  the strips follow the window: turn a phone (or resize) and they move; the reading order matches the drawn order
+//   32e  a category chosen, a ranked save, reduced motion: still a tile on the first screen, the blocks still under the tiles
+//   32f  no sideways scroll on the lobby at ten window sizes, and Stream Mode
+//   32g  the Quests page on a phone: today's and this week's quests come before the 30-row season track; a wide window keeps its order; "Go to my tier" works
+//   32h  axe on the lobby at three sizes
+//
+// What the numbers mean (window = the first screen, scroll at 0):
+//   "a tile on the first screen" = the top of the first game tile + 150 px (its picture) is above the bottom of the window, and, on a phone, above the fixed bottom bar.
+//   "the whole tile" (picture and name) is asked for where it is reachable (all the sizes in WHOLE below). A phone held sideways at 667 x 375 shows the picture and most of the name;
+//   a 320 x 568 phone shows the whole tile; 568 x 320 (a very small phone held sideways) is not asked for (the first tile starts at about 215 px of 320).
+export default async function (h) {
+  const { check, newPage, openApp, go, section, problems, a11y } = h;
+
+  const MAIN = 'givespin:v2';
+  const seeded = async (cents, opts = {}) => {
+    const p = await newPage(opts);
